-- title:
--   A full ℤ-lattice is cut out by its adelic box
-- statement:
--   Let $D$ be a ring equipped with a $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra structure and let $\Lambda$ be a $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule of $D$ which is finitely generated (`hfg`) and whose $\mathbb{Q}$-span is the whole of $D$ (`hspan`); thus $\Lambda$ is a full $\mathbb{Z}$-lattice in $D$, and in particular $D$ is finite-dimensional over $\mathbb{Q}$. Write $\widehat{D} = D \otimes_{\mathbb{Q}} \mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q}}^{f}$ for the tensor product of $D$ with the finite adele ring of $\mathbb{Q}$ (formed with respect to the ring of integers $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$), and let [`Submodule.finiteAdeleBox`](def/Submodule_FiniteAdeleBox.html#L14) $\Lambda$ be the additive subgroup of $\widehat{D}$ generated by the elements $z \otimes a$ with $z \in \Lambda$ and $a$ a finite adele whose component at every height-one prime $v$ of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$ lies in the valuation ring of the $v$-adic completion. For a unit $g$ of $\widehat{D}$, [`Submodule.ofFiniteIdele`](def/Submodule_FiniteAdeleBox.html#L19) $\Lambda\ g$ is the $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule of $D$ obtained by pulling back the left translate $g \cdot$ `finiteAdeleBox` $\Lambda$ along the map $z \mapsto z \otimes 1$. The theorem asserts that for $g = 1$ this submodule is $\Lambda$ itself: $\{\, z \in D : z \otimes 1 \in \widehat{\Lambda} \,\} = \Lambda$.
--
--   This is the statement that a full $\mathbb{Z}$-lattice in a finite-dimensional $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra is recovered as the set of global points of its adelic box, $D \cap \widehat{\Lambda} = \Lambda$, the injectivity half of the lattice–idele dictionary. It is the base case of that dictionary and is used throughout the treatment of Eichler orders and level structures in the Čerednik–Drinfeld material, for instance in identifying the order cut out by a diagonal finite idele.
